<h1>About ToolStack Lab</h1>
<p>ToolStack Lab reviews AI tools the way a working creator uses them: inside real production pipelines, on deadline, with a budget.</p>
<h2>How we test</h2>
<p>Every tool we cover is evaluated on the same five axes: output quality at default settings, output quality after tuning, speed on a realistic batch, pricing at scale (not at the free tier), and what breaks when you push it.</p>
<h2>What we will not do</h2>
<p>We do not publish a review we have not used the tool for. We do not remove a documented downside because a vendor asks. When a tool is wrong for a use case, we say so and name the alternative.</p>
<h2>Editorial independence</h2>
<p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. They never determine the verdict, the ranking, or whether a downside gets published. See our <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Corrections, tips and vendor briefings: <a href="mailto:hello@toolstacklab.com">hello@toolstacklab.com</a>. We publish corrections in place with a dated note.</p>
